# MoOS Mo AI brain — the GPU machine's brain. Qwen3-8B.
#
# WHY A SECOND MODELFILE AND NOT ONE CONSTANT
#
# MoOS runs on two machines that want opposite answers, so moos-ensure-brain
# picks between this file and moai-brain.Modelfile by what the machine has:
#
#   this file            a real GPU with >= 7.5 GB. Qwen3-8B is, MEASURED through
#                        the real gateway on a real Arabic repair question, the
#                        best Arabic of everything tried AND the best at the
#                        commands and explanations that go with it — which is
#                        exactly what a development/repair brain is for.
#   moai-brain.Modelfile no GPU (MoOS Cloud). Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct is measurably
#                        faster there, and Mo AI's own error text says so.
#
# WHY NOT A "CODER" MODEL, WHICH IS THE OBVIOUS THING TO REACH FOR
#
# qwen2.5-coder:7b was tried and REJECTED, and the reason is recorded in
# moai-control so nobody re-adds it on a hunch: it writes excellent one-liners
# and its Arabic is broken — it emitted "الملفات الممكدة" (not a phrase) and
# invented an `lsof -m` flag that does not exist. MoOS's contract is that the
# bilingual UI is not sitting on a monolingual brain. Qwen3 is trained on 119
# languages and does not make that trade.
#
# And qwen3-coder is not an option at all on this card: its smallest tag is the
# 30B-A3B build at ~19 GB of weights, which needs 16 GB+ of VRAM. There is no
# sub-10 GB Qwen3-Coder. On 8 GB it would spill to system RAM, and a spilled
# model on this image does not merely go slow — moos-gpu-headroom exists because
# kwin_wayland died on `NVRM: invalid mmap context` when VRAM ran out.
#
# num_ctx 24576 is NOT a round number, and it is the same contract as the CPU
# Modelfile: the desktop chat sends a short prompt, but the SAME model serves the
# Telegram agent (OpenClaw), whose system+tools prompt ALONE is ~11.5k tokens. At
# 8192 it overflowed before a single user word; at 16384 the first reply worked
# and multi-turn conversations then overran the budget. 24576 leaves ~11k for the
# actual conversation on top of the base prompt. moos-ensure-brain reconciles
# openclaw.json to this value — the two must not drift.
FROM qwen3:8b

# No baked SYSTEM: main.qml sends the real Mo AI system prompt plus live machine
# context, so the model must not carry one of its own. A baked prompt is what
# made an earlier brain answer in Arabic even when asked in English.
SYSTEM ""

PARAMETER num_ctx 24576
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
